---
/**
 * Pricing (MASTER_ROADMAP M22, §9; FUTURE_GATES FG-007, FG-009). A plain
 * statement, deliberately not fictional commerce: no price, plan or
 * entitlement exists, so none is shown.
 */
import MaturityBadge from '../../components/MaturityBadge.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Pricing"
  tag="/pricing/"
  description="SAIPEN is free and open. There is no hosted service and no paid plan today; this page says exactly that."
>
  <h1>Pricing</h1>
  <p><MaturityBadge level="stable" note="a statement of fact, not a price list" /></p>

  <div class="wide-scroll">
    <table class="w-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Offering</th>
          <th scope="col">State</th>
          <th scope="col">What that means today</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Protocol, docs and specification</th>
          <td><span class="w-badge w-badge--ok">free</span></td>
          <td>
            MIT-licensed, <a href={SITE.repository!} rel="noopener" data-external>public on GitHub</a>. Never paywalled,
            never behind an account.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Local and self-hosted use</th>
          <td><span class="w-badge w-badge--ok">free</span></td>
          <td>Everything runs on your machine. There is no entitlement check and none is planned.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Ecosystem tools</th>
          <td><span class="w-badge w-badge--ok">free</span></td>
          <td>The <a href="/ecosystem/">ecosystem</a> projects are public repositories; see each one's licence.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Hosted SAIPEN service</th>
          <td><span class="w-badge w-badge--info">none</span></td>
          <td>Does not exist. No endpoint, account or billing surface.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>If a hosted service ever exists</h2>
  <p>
    It would charge for optional managed infrastructure — hosted execution, persistent shared state, relay, evidence
    retention, observability, organisation controls, support — and never for access to the protocol or its
    specification. The local, open path would not be weakened to push anyone towards it. Until such a service exists,
    this page will not show a monthly price, a seat count or a "contact sales" button.
  </p>

  <h2>Supporting the work</h2>
  <p>
    Support is optional and buys nothing: nothing is locked behind a donation. The author's ways to chip in are listed
    on <a href={SITE.author} rel="noopener" data-external>github.com/vacterro</a>.
  </p>
</SiteLayout>
